From: Elian Doran <doran.adoris.elian@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: gc2145: parallel bus driver from megi's tree

The PinePhone's front camera is a GC2145 on the CSI parallel bus; the
mainline driver only does MIPI CSI-2. This is drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
from Ondrej Jirman's (megi) cams-7.2 branch (https://codeberg.org/megi/linux,
which keeps the mainline one as VIDEO_GC2145_MIPI); only the parallel one is
needed here, so it replaces it. Optional register defaults are read from
gc2145-init.bin when present.

It uses fwnode endpoint parsing and no CCI helpers: Kconfig selects
V4L2_FWNODE instead of V4L2_CCI_I2C.

